- recall_memory
- remember
- flag_for_manual_review
- find_in_trenova
- open_page
- wait_until
- cancel_wait
- search_shipments
- list_shipments
- list_customers
- list_invoices
- list_service_failures
- create_customer
- list_locations
- list_commodities

Callable after find_tools:
- get_shipment — Retrieve one shipment (load) by its id, with its stops, the driver and equipment assigned to each move, the holds on it now and its newest comments.
- add_shipment_comment — Leave a note on a shipment's comment thread, where dispatch will read it.
- list_insights — List insight detector findings: service slipping for a customer, cash tied up in unbilled work, cost leaking at a location, compliance about to lapse.
- get_insight — Read one insight in full: the finding with its numbers and records, its earlier runs, and the rule behind it.
- list_edi_partners — List this organization's EDI trading partners with their code, name and the customer each stands for.
- list_edi_transfers — List EDI load tender transfers, the tenders partners sent in or this organization sent out.
- get_edi_transfer — Retrieve one EDI load tender by id, with its stops, freight and rate and the mappings it still lacks.
- accept_edi_tender — Propose accepting a load tender a trading partner sent over EDI, which creates the shipment from it and tells the partner.
- decline_edi_tender — Propose declining a load tender a trading partner sent over EDI, with the reason they are given.
- list_edi_tender_changes — List changes another Trenova organization made to loads it tendered to this one over EDI, and changes this organization made to loads it tendered, newest first.
- review_edi_tender_change — Propose applying or rejecting a change another Trenova organization made to a load it tendered to this one over EDI, after this organization received it.
- send_edi_status_update — Propose sending a trading partner an EDI 214 shipment status built from a shipment or a service failure.
- list_orders — List customer orders, the commercial record that groups one or more shipments and their charges under a customer's order number, PO or BOL.
- get_order — Retrieve one customer order by id with the shipments it groups and its order-level charges, including which charges are already invoiced.
- create_order — Open a customer order: the commercial record that groups a customer's shipments and order-level charges under their PO or BOL.
- update_order — Change an order's customer, owner, PO number, BOL, currency, quoted amount or base amount.
- attach_order_shipments — Put shipments on an order so they are billed and tracked together.
- detach_order_shipment — Take one shipment off an order onto an order of its own, so it is billed on its own.
- add_order_charge — Add an order-level charge, one billed once for the whole order rather than on a shipment: a consolidation fee, a quoted flat rate.
- update_order_charge — Change an order charge's description, amount or payer split.
- set_order_charge_allocations — Replace how one order charge is split among payers without touching the charge itself.
- remove_order_charge — Take a charge off an order before it is invoiced.
- close_order — Close a Billed order once nothing more will be billed on it.
- cancel_order — Cancel an order and every shipment on it that is not already canceled, with the reason the customer gave.
- list_recurring_shipments — List recurring shipments: the series that copy one saved shipment on a schedule for a customer's standing lane, with when each next generates.
- create_recurring_shipment — Start a recurring shipment: a series that copies one saved shipment on a schedule, for a customer's standing lane.
- update_recurring_shipment — Change a recurring shipment's name, schedule, timezone, dates, limits, blackout days or whether it generates on its own.
- set_recurring_shipment_status — Pause a recurring shipment so it creates nothing, resume it (Active) from its next future slot without back-filling what it missed, or end it (Expired).
- generate_recurring_shipment — Create the shipment for a recurring shipment's next slot now, or for the slot at occurrenceAt, instead of waiting for the schedule.
- rerate_shipment — Price a saved shipment again from its customer's rate agreement, replacing its rating method, base rate and contract accessorials.
- edit_shipment_comment — Change the text, visibility, priority or acknowledgment request of a comment on a shipment.
- unpin_shipment_comment — Take a pinned comment off the top of a shipment's thread once what it said no longer applies.
- delete_shipment_comment — Delete a comment from a shipment's thread: your own, or another person's when the person you act for may moderate comments.
- get_service_failure — Retrieve one service failure by id: the late or missed stop, how late, the reason code, the notes, and who reviewed, resolved or voided it.
- update_service_failure — Change the reason code, notes or EDI 214 code overrides on an open or reviewed service failure.
- review_service_failure — Mark an open service failure reviewed, with the reason code that explains it, once a person has looked into what happened.
- void_service_failure — Void a service failure that should never have been opened, with the reason why: a wrong appointment window, a corrected arrival, a stop that was not late.
- dispute_detention — Record that the customer disputes a detention charge, with what they said.
- vet_customer_broker — Check a customer that is a freight broker against the public FMCSA record by its DOT number: broker authority and bond.
- update_customer — Change a customer's details: name, billing address, DOT and MC numbers, who is emailed status updates, and consolidation.
- update_customer_status — Set one or more customers Active or Inactive, which decides whether shipments can be booked for them.
- update_location — Change a location's name, description, address or category.
- update_location_status — Set one or more locations Active or Inactive, which decides whether stops can be booked at them.
- create_commodity — Add a commodity shipments can carry, with its freight class, temperature range, dimensions and handling.
- update_commodity — Change a commodity: its name, description, freight class, temperature range, dimensions, handling or hazardous material.

How a task is done with these, in order, each step's result feeding the next; skip a step whose answer you already have:
- accept_edi_tender: list_edi_transfers → get_edi_transfer → get_customer → search_shipments → quote_shipment → accept_edi_tender
- decline_edi_tender: list_edi_transfers → get_edi_transfer → decline_edi_tender
- review_edi_tender_change: list_edi_tender_changes → review_edi_tender_change
